# .helmcheckignore — check-helm-values-keys.sh baseline for infrastructure/kyverno
# (kyverno/kyverno chart, pinned in kustomization.yaml).
#
# One key path per line; `#` comments and blanks ignored. An entry `a.b`
# acknowledges `a.b` and every key nested under it (`a.b.*`). With this file
# present the layer is GATED: any key not in the chart's values tree and not
# listed here blocks the commit.
#
# Why this file exists (2026-09-14): `admissionController.resources` sat in
# values.yaml from the ADR 0036 rollout and rendered to nothing — the chart
# reads `admissionController.container.resources` — so the live admission
# controller ran on the chart-default 384Mi limit while the comment claimed
# 1Gi. The hook flagged the key all along; the layer just had no baseline, so
# the flag was a warning nobody read. Triage method for a new flag:
# `grep -rn '.Values.<key>' infrastructure/kyverno/charts/*/` — chart reads it
# → back-compat-OK below; it doesn't → real dropped wrong-key, fix values.yaml.

# ── Back-compat-OK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# List-item subpaths: the chart's defaults are empty lists (`[]`), so the
# item keys never appear in `helm show values`, but the templates `toYaml`/
# `range` over them and they render correctly.
admissionController.extraVolumes             # chart: `with .Values.admissionController.extraVolumes`
admissionController.extraVolumeMounts        # chart: `with .Values.admissionController.extraVolumeMounts`
admissionController.topologySpreadConstraints  # chart: `with .Values.admissionController.topologySpreadConstraints`
backgroundController.extraVolumes
backgroundController.extraVolumeMounts
backgroundController.topologySpreadConstraints
cleanupController.topologySpreadConstraints
reportsController.extraVolumes
reportsController.extraVolumeMounts
reportsController.topologySpreadConstraints
reportsController.rbac.clusterRole.extraResources  # chart: `range .Values.reportsController.rbac.clusterRole.extraResources`
# Free-form label maps: the chart default is `{}` and the template `toYaml`s
# whatever is set, so the label KEY we choose (`release`) is never in the tree.
admissionController.serviceMonitor.additionalLabels
backgroundController.serviceMonitor.additionalLabels
cleanupController.serviceMonitor.additionalLabels
reportsController.serviceMonitor.additionalLabels

# ── KNOWN WRONG-KEYS — value is DROPPED at render ────────────────────────────
# (none — admissionController.resources was fixed, not suppressed, 2026-09-14)
